  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "b-hB5im5Jg1vJwrzq9l6v",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 242.83853149414062,
      "y": 128.0078125,
      "width": 1459.3229675292969,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 652795569,
      "version": 2220,
      "versionNonce": 15073585,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792837163474,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Functional Requirements :\n    1. Given a user, synchronise application configurations like prefrences, game state, UI settings accross multiple personal devices.\n    2. Support full offline functionality so that device must be able to read and modify cofigurations locally without an internet connection, queuing\nupdates for later.\n    3. Automatically handles concurrent or conflicting updats made on different devies while offline or online.\n    4. When a user has multiple devices online an update on one device should reflect on others with minimal delay.\n\n2. Non - Functional Requirements :\n    1. High availability - 99.99% for core sync\n    2. Eventual consistency across all devices\n    3. Efficient bandwidth\n    4. Low latency for real time online updates\n\n3. Back of the envelope :\n    - Scale : 100M active users, avg 3 device / user = 300 M devices\n    - Storage : Avg configuration payload = 10kb / user => 100M users * 10kb = 1 TB of active configuration data.\n    - Read QPS : 5 syncs / day / device = 1.5B syncs / day = ~ 17,000 QPS avg => peak = 50,000\n    - Write QPS : 1 config change / day = ~1200 writes QPS\n\n4. API designing : \n    1. Sync config : Pull and Push : POST /api/v1/sync\n        payload - {\"user_id\" : ...., \"device_id\" : ....., \"client_version\": ....,}\n    2. Websocket Connection : wss : //ws.domain.com/v1/stream?device_id={device_id}\n\n5. Data models and entities:\n    1. user_config : -user_id, config_key, config_value, updated_at, version - Cassandra or DynamoDB\n    2. Redis as Hot storage Key : user_id, Value : Hash containing latest config state and latest version\n    3. Clinet side storage : pending_mutations : SQLite or Room or Core data\n\n6. High level Diagram : \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Functional Requirements :\n    1. Given a user, synchronise application configurations like prefrences, game state, UI settings accross multiple personal devices.\n    2. Support full offline functionality so that device must be able to read and modify cofigurations locally without an internet connection, queuing updates for later.\n    3. Automatically handles concurrent or conflicting updats made on different devies while offline or online.\n    4. When a user has multiple devices online an update on one device should reflect on others with minimal delay.\n\n2. Non - Functional Requirements :\n    1. High availability - 99.99% for core sync\n    2. Eventual consistency across all devices\n    3. Efficient bandwidth\n    4. Low latency for real time online updates\n\n3. Back of the envelope :\n    - Scale : 100M active users, avg 3 device / user = 300 M devices\n    - Storage : Avg configuration payload = 10kb / user => 100M users * 10kb = 1 TB of active configuration data.\n    - Read QPS : 5 syncs / day / device = 1.5B syncs / day = ~ 17,000 QPS avg => peak = 50,000\n    - Write QPS : 1 config change / day = ~1200 writes QPS\n\n4. API designing : \n    1. Sync config : Pull and Push : POST /api/v1/sync\n        payload - {\"user_id\" : ...., \"device_id\" : ....., \"client_version\": ....,}\n    2. Websocket Connection : wss : //ws.domain.com/v1/stream?device_id={device_id}\n\n5. Data models and entities:\n    1. user_config : -user_id, config_key, config_value, updated_at, version - Cassandra or DynamoDB\n    2. Redis as Hot storage Key : user_id, Value : Hash containing latest config state and latest version\n    3. Clinet side storage : pending_mutations : SQLite or Room or Core data\n\n6. High level Diagram : \n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
